IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- sections 28 to 34: rents paid in good faith, improvements by bona fide holders, double rent on holding over,
-- the subtenant's notice; the State Courts; presumption of survivorship; accumulation of income; the perpetuity period;
-- powers of appointment; wait and see.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer".
-- "Forthwith" (s 28(5)) is left to the caller as a yes/no input: the Act defines no period for it.

§ `Section 28(1) to (3) -- rents paid in good faith; improvements by bona fide holders`

-- src:1699 | 28.—(1) No person shall be chargeable with any rents or profits of
-- src:1700 | any immovable property which he has bona fide paid over to any
-- src:1701 | person of whom he bona fide held the rents or profits notwithstanding
-- src:1702 | it afterwards appears that the person to whom such payment was
-- src:1703 | made had no right to receive the rents or profits.
@ref s 28(1) (src:1699-1703)
GIVEN `he has bona fide paid the rents or profits over to a person of whom he bona fide held them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it afterwards appears that the person to whom the payment was made had no right to receive them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) the person is chargeable with the rents or profits of the immovable property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `he has bona fide paid the rents or profits over to a person of whom he bona fide held them` AND `it afterwards appears that the person to whom the payment was made had no right to receive them` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be chargeable with any rents or profits of any immovable property which he has bona fide paid over to any person of whom he bona fide held the rents or profits notwithstanding it afterwards appears that the person to whom such payment was made had no right to receive the rents or profits"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any rents or profits ... which he has bona fide paid over to any person of whom he bona fide held the rents or profits"

-- src:1707 | (2) If any person erects any building or makes an improvement
-- src:1708 | upon any lands held by him bona fide in the belief that he had an
-- src:1709 | estate in fee simple or other absolute estate, and that person, his
-- src:1710 | executor or assign, or his under‑tenant is evicted from such lands by
-- src:1711 | any person having a better title, the person who erected the building
-- src:1712 | or made the improvement, his executor or assign, shall be entitled —
-- src:1714 | (a) to have the value of the building or improvement so erected
-- src:1715 | or made during such holding and in such belief estimated
-- src:1716 | and paid or secured to him; or
@ref s 28(2)(a) (src:1707-1716)
GIVEN `the person erected a building or made an improvement upon lands held by him bona fide in the belief that he had an estate in fee simple or other absolute estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he or his executor or assign or his under-tenant is evicted from the lands by a person having a better title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(2)(a) the person is entitled to have the value of the building or improvement estimated and paid or secured to him` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person erected a building or made an improvement upon lands held by him bona fide in the belief that he had an estate in fee simple or other absolute estate` AND `he or his executor or assign or his under-tenant is evicted from the lands by a person having a better title` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any person erects any building or makes an improvement upon any lands held by him bona fide in the belief that he had an estate in fee simple or other absolute estate, and that person ... is evicted from such lands by any person having a better title, the person who erected the building or made the improvement ... shall be entitled" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "if" is the text's no

-- src:1707 | (2) If any person erects any building or makes an improvement
-- src:1708 | upon any lands held by him bona fide in the belief that he had an
-- src:1709 | estate in fee simple or other absolute estate, and that person, his
-- src:1710 | executor or assign, or his under‑tenant is evicted from such lands by
-- src:1711 | any person having a better title, the person who erected the building
-- src:1712 | or made the improvement, his executor or assign, shall be entitled —
-- src:1718 | (b) at the option of the person causing the eviction, to purchase
-- src:1719 | the interest of such person in the lands at the value thereof
-- src:1720 | irrespective of the value of the building or improvement.
@ref s 28(2)(b) (src:1707-1720)
GIVEN `the person erected a building or made an improvement upon lands held by him bona fide in the belief that he had an estate in fee simple or other absolute estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he or his executor or assign or his under-tenant is evicted from the lands by a person having a better title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person causing the eviction exercises his option` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(2)(b) the person is entitled to purchase the interest of the person causing the eviction in the lands at their value irrespective of the building or improvement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person erected a building or made an improvement upon lands held by him bona fide in the belief that he had an estate in fee simple or other absolute estate` AND `he or his executor or assign or his under-tenant is evicted from the lands by a person having a better title`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any person erects any building or makes an improvement upon any lands held by him bona fide ... and that person ... is evicted ... the person who erected the building or made the improvement ... shall be entitled" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "if" is the text's no
        IF `the person causing the eviction exercises his option` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the option of the person causing the eviction"

-- src:1727 | (3) The amount to be paid or secured in respect of such building or
-- src:1728 | improvement shall be the estimated value of the building and
-- src:1729 | improvement at the time of such eviction.
@ref s 28(3) (src:1727-1729)
GIVEN `the amount is the amount to be paid or secured in respect of the building or improvement under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3) the amount is the estimated value of the building and improvement at the time of the eviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount is the amount to be paid or secured in respect of the building or improvement under subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The amount to be paid or secured in respect of such building or improvement"

-- src:1727 | (3) The amount to be paid or secured in respect of such building or
-- src:1728 | improvement shall be the estimated value of the building and
-- src:1729 | improvement at the time of such eviction.
@ref s 28(3) the amount (src:1727-1729)
GIVEN `the amount is the amount to be paid or secured in respect of the building or improvement under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estimated value of the building and improvement at the time of the eviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 28(3) the amount to be paid or secured` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 28(3) the amount is the estimated value of the building and improvement at the time of the eviction` `the amount is the amount to be paid or secured in respect of the building or improvement under subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the estimated value of the building and improvement at the time of the eviction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The amount to be paid or secured in respect of such building or improvement"; see the companion s 28(3) the amount is the estimated value of the building and improvement at the time of the eviction

§ `Section 28(4) and (5) -- holding over; the subtenant`

-- src:1733 | (4) Every tenant holding over after the determination of his tenancy
-- src:1734 | shall be chargeable, at the option of his landlord, with double the
-- src:1735 | amount of his rent until possession is given up by him or with double
-- src:1736 | the value during the period of detention of the land or premises so
-- src:1737 | detained, whether notice to that effect has been given or not.
@ref s 28(4) double rent (src:1733-1737)
GIVEN `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the landlord opts for double the amount of the rent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the amount of his rent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every tenant holding over after the determination of his tenancy"
        IF `the landlord opts for double the amount of the rent` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the option of his landlord"

-- src:1733 | (4) Every tenant holding over after the determination of his tenancy
-- src:1734 | shall be chargeable, at the option of his landlord, with double the
-- src:1735 | amount of his rent until possession is given up by him or with double
-- src:1736 | the value during the period of detention of the land or premises so
-- src:1737 | detained, whether notice to that effect has been given or not.
@ref s 28(4) double value (src:1733-1737)
GIVEN `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the landlord opts for double the value during the period of detention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the value during the period of detention` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every tenant holding over after the determination of his tenancy"
        IF `the landlord opts for double the value during the period of detention` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the option of his landlord"

-- src:1733 | (4) Every tenant holding over after the determination of his tenancy
-- src:1734 | shall be chargeable, at the option of his landlord, with double the
-- src:1735 | amount of his rent until possession is given up by him or with double
-- src:1736 | the value during the period of detention of the land or premises so
-- src:1737 | detained, whether notice to that effect has been given or not.
@ref s 28(4) the sum (src:1733-1737)
GIVEN `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the landlord opts for double the amount of the rent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rent for the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 28(4) double the amount of the rent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the amount of his rent` `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` `the landlord opts for double the amount of the rent` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST (2 TIMES `the rent for the period`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the option of his landlord"; see the companion s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the amount of his rent

-- src:1735 | amount of his rent until possession is given up by him or with double
-- src:1736 | the value during the period of detention of the land or premises so
-- src:1737 | detained, whether notice to that effect has been given or not.
@ref s 28(4) until possession is given up (src:1735-1737)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the tenancy was determined` IS A DATE
      `the date on which possession is given up` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(4) the day falls within the period for which double rent or double value is chargeable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the day` AT LEAST (`the date on which the tenancy was determined` PLUS 1)) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every tenant holding over after the determination of his tenancy" -- the period begins the day after the tenancy is determined (fork F-P2)
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the date on which possession is given up`
            WHEN JUST given THEN
                IF `the day` AT MOST given THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until possession is given up by him" -- the day possession is given up is the last day charged (fork F-P3)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:1735 | amount of his rent until possession is given up by him or with double
-- src:1736 | the value during the period of detention of the land or premises so
-- src:1737 | detained, whether notice to that effect has been given or not.
@ref s 28(4) notice (src:1735-1737)
GIVEN `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(4) notice that the landlord opts is a condition of the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whether notice to that effect has been given or not"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every tenant holding over after the determination of his tenancy"

-- src:1741 | (5) When any originating claim issued by a landlord against a
-- src:1742 | tenant for the recovery of immovable property is served on or comes
-- src:1743 | to the knowledge of any subtenant of the claimant’s immediate
-- src:1744 | tenant, the subtenant being an occupier of the whole or any part of the
-- src:1745 | premises sought to be recovered, he shall forthwith give notice
-- src:1746 | thereof to his immediate landlord, under penalty of forfeiting 3 years’
-- src:1747 | rack rent of the premises held by the subtenant to the person of whom
-- src:1748 | he holds, to be recovered by such person by action in any court having
-- src:1749 | jurisdiction.
@ref s 28(5) the duty arises (src:1741-1749)
GIVEN `an originating claim issued by a landlord against a tenant for the recovery of immovable property is served on or comes to the knowledge of the subtenant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a subtenant of the claimant's immediate tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subtenant is an occupier of the whole or any part of the premises sought to be recovered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(5) the duty of the subtenant to give notice to his immediate landlord arises` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an originating claim issued by a landlord against a tenant for the recovery of immovable property is served on or comes to the knowledge of the subtenant` AND `the person is a subtenant of the claimant's immediate tenant` AND `the subtenant is an occupier of the whole or any part of the premises sought to be recovered` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When any originating claim issued by a landlord against a tenant for the recovery of immovable property is served on or comes to the knowledge of any subtenant of the claimant's immediate tenant, the subtenant being an occupier of the whole or any part of the premises sought to be recovered, he shall forthwith give notice" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "when" is read as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling)

@ref s 28(5) compliance (src:1741-1749)
GIVEN `the duty arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subtenant has given notice of the originating claim to his immediate landlord forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(5) the subtenant has given notice to his immediate landlord forthwith` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the duty arises` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "When any originating claim ... is served on or comes to the knowledge of any subtenant" -- the duty does not arise; the companion s 28(5) the duty of the subtenant to give notice to his immediate landlord arises answers that (fork QD)
        IF `the subtenant has given notice of the originating claim to his immediate landlord forthwith` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "shall" (fork QB); the subsection states the penalty (forfeiture of 3 years' rack rent), see s 28(5) the sum forfeited, and "forthwith" is not defined

@ref s 28(5) as a regulative rule (src:1741-1749)
GIVEN `the duty arises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under section 28(5)` `Act under section 28(5)`
`s 28(5) the subtenant must give notice of the originating claim to his immediate landlord` MEANS
    IF `the duty arises`
    THEN
        PARTY `The subtenant`
        MUST `give notice of the originating claim to his immediate landlord`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `The subtenant` BECAUSE "notice of the originating claim not given forthwith to his immediate landlord (s 28(5)); the subtenant forfeits 3 years' rack rent of the premises he holds"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:1746 | thereof to his immediate landlord, under penalty of forfeiting 3 years’
-- src:1747 | rack rent of the premises held by the subtenant to the person of whom
-- src:1748 | he holds, to be recovered by such person by action in any court having
-- src:1749 | jurisdiction.
@ref s 28(5) the sum forfeited (src:1746-1749)
GIVEN `the subtenant failed to give notice forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the yearly rack rent of the premises held by the subtenant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 28(5) the sum forfeited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the subtenant failed to give notice forthwith` THEN JUST (3 TIMES `the yearly rack rent of the premises held by the subtenant`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under penalty of forfeiting 3 years' rack rent"

-- src:1746 | thereof to his immediate landlord, under penalty of forfeiting 3 years’
-- src:1747 | rack rent of the premises held by the subtenant to the person of whom
-- src:1748 | he holds, to be recovered by such person by action in any court having
-- src:1749 | jurisdiction.
@ref s 28(5) the penalty applies (src:1746-1749)
GIVEN `the subtenant failed to give notice forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(5) the subtenant forfeits 3 years' rack rent to the person of whom he holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the subtenant failed to give notice forthwith` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "under penalty of forfeiting 3 years' rack rent of the premises held by the subtenant" -- a penalty for a failure that did not occur does not arise (MARGINAL (a))

§ `Section 29 -- rules to apply to the State Courts`

-- src:1755 | 29. The rules of law enacted in this Act and declared shall with the
-- src:1756 | necessary modifications be, and shall, so far as they were already in
-- src:1757 | force in Singapore, be deemed to have been, in force in the State
-- src:1758 | Courts so far as the matters to which such rules relate are respectively
-- src:1759 | cognizable by such courts.
@ref s 29 (src:1755-1759)
GIVEN `the matters to which the rule relates are cognizable by the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29 the rule of law enacted in this Act is in force in the State Courts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matters to which the rule relates are cognizable by the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so far as the matters to which such rules relate are respectively cognizable by such courts"

-- src:1755 | 29. The rules of law enacted in this Act and declared shall with the
-- src:1756 | necessary modifications be, and shall, so far as they were already in
-- src:1757 | force in Singapore, be deemed to have been, in force in the State
-- src:1758 | Courts so far as the matters to which such rules relate are respectively
-- src:1759 | cognizable by such courts.
@ref s 29 the deeming for the past (src:1755-1759)
GIVEN `the rule was already in force in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matters to which the rule relates are cognizable by the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29 the rule is deemed to have been in force in the State Courts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the rule was already in force in Singapore` AND `the matters to which the rule relates are cognizable by the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so far as they were already in force in Singapore" and "so far as the matters to which such rules relate are respectively cognizable by such courts"

§ `Section 30 -- presumption of survivorship in regard to claim to property`

-- src:1765 | 30. In all cases where 2 or more persons die in circumstances
-- src:1766 | rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other or others,
-- src:1767 | such deaths shall (subject to any order of the court) for all purposes
-- src:1768 | affecting the title to property be presumed to have occurred in order
-- src:1773 | of seniority and accordingly the younger shall be deemed to have
-- src:1774 | survived the elder.
@ref s 30 (src:1765-1774)
GIVEN `2 or more persons die in circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other or others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose affects the title to property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has made an order to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30 the deaths are presumed to have occurred in order of seniority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `2 or more persons die in circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other or others` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In all cases where 2 or more persons die in circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other or others, such deaths shall ... be presumed to have occurred in order of seniority" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))
        IF NOT `the purpose affects the title to property` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for all purposes affecting the title to property"
        IF `the court has made an order to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(subject to any order of the court)" -- an exception to a presumption: the presumption does not apply
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1765 | 30. In all cases where 2 or more persons die in circumstances
-- src:1766 | rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other or others,
-- src:1767 | such deaths shall (subject to any order of the court) for all purposes
-- src:1768 | affecting the title to property be presumed to have occurred in order
-- src:1773 | of seniority and accordingly the younger shall be deemed to have
-- src:1774 | survived the elder.
@ref s 30 the younger (src:1765-1774)
GIVEN `2 or more persons die in circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other or others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose affects the title to property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has made an order to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of birth of the first person` IS A DATE
      `the date of birth of the second person` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30 the first person is deemed to have survived the second` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 30 the deaths are presumed to have occurred in order of seniority` `2 or more persons die in circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other or others` `the purpose affects the title to property` `the court has made an order to the contrary` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the presumption does not apply on these facts; see the companion s 30 the deaths are presumed to have occurred in order of seniority
        IF `the date of birth of the first person` GREATER THAN `the date of birth of the second person` THEN JUST TRUE -- "the younger shall be deemed to have survived the elder"
        IF `the date of birth of the first person` LESS THAN `the date of birth of the second person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the younger shall be deemed to have survived the elder" -- the elder is not deemed to have survived the younger
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two persons of the same age: the Act says nothing of equal seniority

§ `Section 31 -- accumulation of income`

-- src:1778 | 31.—(1) Income arising from a settlement or disposition of
-- src:1779 | property made on or after 15 December 2004 may, subject to the
-- src:1780 | terms of the settlement or disposition to the contrary, be accumulated
-- src:1781 | for the duration of the settlement or disposition.
@ref s 31(1) (src:1778-1781)
GIVEN `the date on which the settlement or disposition was made` IS A DATE
      `the terms of the settlement or disposition provide to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accumulation is for the duration of the settlement or disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the income may be accumulated for the duration of the settlement or disposition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date on which the settlement or disposition was made` AT LEAST (Date 15 12 2004)) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a settlement or disposition of property made on or after 15 December 2004"; subsection (2) deals with an earlier one
        IF `the terms of the settlement or disposition provide to the contrary` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the terms of the settlement or disposition to the contrary" -- a lifted permission grants nothing (fork QA)
        IF `the accumulation is for the duration of the settlement or disposition` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "be accumulated for the duration of the settlement or disposition" -- a period fixed in the text's own words (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

-- src:1785 | (2) Except as otherwise provided in subsection (4), income arising
-- src:1786 | from a settlement or disposition of property made before
-- src:1787 | 15 December 2004 shall not be wholly or partially accumulated for
-- src:1788 | any longer period than one of the following, namely:
-- src:1790 | (a) the life of the grantor or settlor;
-- src:1792 | (b) a term of 21 years from the death of the grantor, settlor or
-- src:1793 | testator;
-- src:1795 | (c) the duration of the minority or respective minorities of any
-- src:1796 | person or persons living or en ventre sa mere at the death of
-- src:1797 | the grantor, settlor or testator;
-- src:1799 | (d) the duration of the minority or respective minorities only of
-- src:1800 | any person or persons who under the limitations of the
-- src:1801 | instrument directing the accumulations would, for the time
-- src:1802 | being, if of full age, be entitled to the income directed to be
-- src:1803 | accumulated;
-- src:1805 | (e) a term of 21 years from the date of the making of the
-- src:1806 | disposition; or
-- src:1808 | (f) the duration of the minority or respective minorities of any
-- src:1809 | person or persons in being at the date of the making of the
-- src:1810 | disposition.
@ref s 31(2) (src:1785-1810)
GIVEN `the date on which the settlement or disposition was made` IS A DATE
      `the period of accumulation` IS A `Period of accumulation`
      `the provision is one to which subsection (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date on which the settlement or disposition was made` AT LEAST (Date 15 12 2004) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a settlement or disposition of property made before 15 December 2004"; subsection (1) deals with a later one
        IF `the provision is one to which subsection (4) applies` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as otherwise provided in subsection (4)" -- a lifted bar grants nothing (fork QA); see s 31(4)
        IF `the period of accumulation` EQUALS `None of these periods` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be wholly or partially accumulated for any longer period than one of the following, namely"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1792 | (b) a term of 21 years from the death of the grantor, settlor or
-- src:1793 | testator;
@ref s 31(2)(b) the last day of the term of 21 years from the death (src:1792-1793)
GIVEN `the date of the death of the grantor settlor or testator` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 31(2)(b) the last day of the term of 21 years from the death` MEANS
    -- The Act gives no rule for counting "a term of 21 years from" a day; the Interpretation Act module (copied unchanged) defines "year" and applies s 50(b) to a last day worked out elsewhere,
    -- so this is the row's convention for months and years (forks F-M1, F-IA1): 252 calendar months after the death on the same day of the month, then s 50(b).  The death day is not counted ("from").
    -- Fork F-S31-21: s 50(b) is applied to the end of a term of property, not only to a time for doing an act; the other reading ends the term on the anniversary itself.
    `the last day of the period once section 50(b) is applied` (`add months` `the date of the death of the grantor settlor or testator` 252) Years `the public holidays` FALSE

-- src:1792 | (b) a term of 21 years from the death of the grantor, settlor or
-- src:1793 | testator;
@ref s 31(2)(b) whether a day falls within the term of 21 years from the death (src:1792-1793)
GIVEN `the date of the death of the grantor settlor or testator` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2)(b) the day falls within the term of 21 years from the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 31(2)(b) the last day of the term of 21 years from the death` `the date of the death of the grantor settlor or testator` `the public holidays`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act module found a contrary intention, which this encoding never passes
    WHEN JUST lastday THEN
        IF `the day asked about` AT LEAST (`the date of the death of the grantor settlor or testator` PLUS 1) AND `the day asked about` AT MOST lastday
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a term of 21 years from the death of the grantor, settlor or testator" -- a period fixed in the text's own words (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

-- src:1814 | (3) In every case where any accumulation is directed otherwise than
-- src:1815 | in accordance with subsection (2), the direction shall, except as
-- src:1816 | otherwise provided in subsection (4), be void, and the income of the
-- src:1817 | property directed to be accumulated shall, so long as the same is
-- src:1818 | directed to be accumulated contrary to this section, go to and be
-- src:1823 | received by the person or persons who would have been entitled
-- src:1824 | thereto if such accumulation had not been directed.
@ref s 31(3) the direction (src:1814-1824)
GIVEN `the accumulation is directed otherwise than in accordance with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is one to which subsection (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(3) the direction is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accumulation is directed otherwise than in accordance with subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In every case where any accumulation is directed otherwise than in accordance with subsection (2), the direction shall ... be void" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))
        IF `the provision is one to which subsection (4) applies` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except as otherwise provided in subsection (4)" -- an exception to a nullity: the requirement does not apply
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1816 | otherwise provided in subsection (4), be void, and the income of the
-- src:1817 | property directed to be accumulated shall, so long as the same is
-- src:1818 | directed to be accumulated contrary to this section, go to and be
-- src:1823 | received by the person or persons who would have been entitled
-- src:1824 | thereto if such accumulation had not been directed.
@ref s 31(3) the income (src:1816-1824)
GIVEN `the accumulation is directed contrary to section 31` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is one to which subsection (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(3) the income goes to the persons who would have been entitled if the accumulation had not been directed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accumulation is directed contrary to section 31` AND (NOT `the provision is one to which subsection (4) applies`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as the same is directed to be accumulated contrary to this section, go to and be received by the person or persons who would have been entitled thereto if such accumulation had not been directed"

-- src:1828 | (4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not extend to any provision —
-- src:1830 | (a) for payment of the debts of any grantor, settlor, testator or
-- src:1831 | other person; or
-- src:1833 | (b) for raising portions for —
-- src:1835 | (i) any child, children or remoter issue of any grantor,
-- src:1836 | settlor or testator; or
-- src:1838 | (ii) any child, children or remoter issue of a person
-- src:1839 | taking any interest under any settlement or other
-- src:1840 | disposition directing the accumulations or to whom
-- src:1841 | any interest is thereby limited,
@ref s 31(4) (src:1828-1841)
GIVEN `the provision is for payment of the debts of a grantor settlor testator or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is for raising portions for a child children or remoter issue of a grantor settlor or testator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is for raising portions for a child children or remoter issue of a person taking an interest under the settlement or to whom any interest is limited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(4) subsections (2) and (3) extend to the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision is for payment of the debts of a grantor settlor testator or other person` OR `the provision is for raising portions for a child children or remoter issue of a grantor settlor or testator` OR `the provision is for raising portions for a child children or remoter issue of a person taking an interest under the settlement or to whom any interest is limited` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2) and (3) do not extend to any provision — (a) for payment of the debts of any grantor, settlor, testator or other person; or (b) for raising portions for — (i) any child, children or remoter issue of any grantor, settlor or testator; or (ii) any child, children or remoter issue of a person taking any interest under any settlement"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names two kinds of provision it does not reach and says nothing of any other

-- src:1828 | (4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not extend to any provision —
-- src:1843 | and accordingly such provisions may be made as if no statutory
-- src:1844 | restrictions on accumulation of income had been imposed.
@ref s 31(4) accordingly (src:1828-1844)
GIVEN `the provision is one to which subsection (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(4) the provision may be made as if no statutory restrictions on accumulation of income had been imposed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision is one to which subsection (4) applies` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and accordingly such provisions may be made"

§ `Sections 32 to 34 -- the perpetuity period, powers of appointment, wait and see`

-- src:1850 | 32.—(1) In the rule against perpetuities as is applicable to any
-- src:1851 | settlement or disposition of property, the perpetuity period shall be
-- src:1852 | 100 years or such shorter period as may be specified in the instrument
-- src:1853 | by which the settlement or disposition is made.
@ref s 32(1) (src:1850-1853)
GIVEN `the rule against perpetuities is applicable to the settlement or disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) the perpetuity period is 100 years or the shorter period specified in the instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the rule against perpetuities is applicable to the settlement or disposition` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the rule against perpetuities as is applicable to any settlement or disposition of property"

-- src:1850 | 32.—(1) In the rule against perpetuities as is applicable to any
-- src:1851 | settlement or disposition of property, the perpetuity period shall be
-- src:1852 | 100 years or such shorter period as may be specified in the instrument
-- src:1853 | by which the settlement or disposition is made.
-- src:1857 | (2) Where any instrument making any settlement or disposition of
-- src:1858 | property refers to lives in being or specifies a perpetuity period that
-- src:1859 | exceeds 100 years, the perpetuity period shall be deemed to be a
-- src:1860 | period of 100 years.
@ref s 32(1) and (2) the period in years (src:1850-1860)
GIVEN `the rule against perpetuities is applicable to the settlement or disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument refers to lives in being` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period specified in the instrument` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 32 the perpetuity period in years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 32(1) the perpetuity period is 100 years or the shorter period specified in the instrument` `the rule against perpetuities is applicable to the settlement or disposition` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the rule against perpetuities as is applicable to any settlement or disposition of property"
        IF `the instrument refers to lives in being` THEN JUST 100 -- s 32(2): "the perpetuity period shall be deemed to be a period of 100 years"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the period specified in the instrument`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 100
            WHEN JUST years THEN JUST (min 100 years)

-- src:1857 | (2) Where any instrument making any settlement or disposition of
-- src:1858 | property refers to lives in being or specifies a perpetuity period that
-- src:1859 | exceeds 100 years, the perpetuity period shall be deemed to be a
-- src:1860 | period of 100 years.
@ref s 32(2) (src:1857-1860)
GIVEN `the instrument refers to lives in being` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument specifies a perpetuity period that exceeds 100 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the perpetuity period is deemed to be a period of 100 years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the instrument refers to lives in being` OR `the instrument specifies a perpetuity period that exceeds 100 years` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any instrument making any settlement or disposition of property refers to lives in being or specifies a perpetuity period that exceeds 100 years, the perpetuity period shall be deemed to be a period of 100 years" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no

-- src:1864 | (3) This section shall apply in relation to —
-- src:1866 | (a) any instrument made in the exercise of a special power of
-- src:1867 | appointment where the instrument creating the special
-- src:1868 | power of appointment takes effect on or after 15 December
-- src:1869 | 2004; and
-- src:1874 | (b) any other instrument taking effect on or after 15 December
-- src:1875 | 2004.
@ref s 32(3) (src:1864-1875)
GIVEN `the instrument is made in the exercise of a special power of appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the instrument creating the special power takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the instrument takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(3) section 32 applies in relation to the instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the instrument is made in the exercise of a special power of appointment` AND `the date on which the instrument creating the special power takes effect` AT LEAST (Date 15 12 2004) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (NOT `the instrument is made in the exercise of a special power of appointment`) AND `the date on which the instrument takes effect` AT LEAST (Date 15 12 2004) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) any instrument made in the exercise of a special power of appointment where the instrument creating the special power of appointment takes effect on or after 15 December 2004; and (b) any other instrument taking effect on or after 15 December 2004"

-- src:1881 | 33.—(1) For the purposes of section 32, a power of appointment
-- src:1882 | shall be treated as a special power unless —
-- src:1884 | (a) in the instrument creating the power it is expressed to be
-- src:1885 | exercisable by one person only; and
-- src:1887 | (b) it could, at all times during its currency when that person is
-- src:1888 | of full age and capacity, be exercised by him so as
-- src:1889 | immediately to transfer to himself the whole of the interest
-- src:1890 | governed by the power without the consent of any other
-- src:1891 | person or compliance with any other condition, not being a
-- src:1892 | formal condition relating only to the mode of exercise of
-- src:1893 | the power.
@ref s 33(1) (src:1881-1893)
GIVEN `it is expressed in the instrument creating the power to be exercisable by one person only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it could at all times during its currency when that person is of full age and capacity be exercised by him so as immediately to transfer to himself the whole of the interest governed by the power without the consent of any other person or compliance with any other condition not being a formal condition relating only to the mode of exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(1) the power of appointment is treated as a special power` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is expressed in the instrument creating the power to be exercisable by one person only` AND `it could at all times during its currency when that person is of full age and capacity be exercised by him so as immediately to transfer to himself the whole of the interest governed by the power without the consent of any other person or compliance with any other condition not being a formal condition relating only to the mode of exercise` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a power of appointment shall be treated as a special power unless — (a) in the instrument creating the power it is expressed to be exercisable by one person only; and (b) it could, at all times during its currency ..., be exercised by him so as immediately to transfer to himself the whole of the interest governed by the power" -- an exception to a deeming: the requirement does not apply
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1897 | (2) For the purpose of determining whether a disposition made
-- src:1898 | under a power of appointment exercisable by will only is void for
-- src:1899 | remoteness, the power shall be treated as a general power where it
-- src:1900 | would have fallen to be so treated if exercisable by deed.
@ref s 33(2) (src:1897-1900)
GIVEN `the purpose is to determine whether a disposition made under a power of appointment exercisable by will only is void for remoteness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power would have fallen to be treated as a general power if exercisable by deed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(2) the power exercisable by will only is treated as a general power` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the purpose is to determine whether a disposition made under a power of appointment exercisable by will only is void for remoteness` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of determining whether a disposition made under a power of appointment exercisable by will only is void for remoteness"
        IF `the power would have fallen to be treated as a general power if exercisable by deed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the power shall be treated as a general power where it would have fallen to be so treated if exercisable by deed" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))

-- src:1906 | 34.—(1) Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a
-- src:1907 | disposition would be invalid as infringing the rule against
-- src:1908 | perpetuities, the disposition shall be treated, until such time (if
-- src:1909 | any) as it becomes certain that the vesting will occur, if at all, after the
-- src:1910 | end of the perpetuity period, as if the disposition were not invalid as
-- src:1911 | infringing the rule against perpetuities, and its becoming so certain
-- src:1912 | shall not affect the validity of anything previously done in relation to
-- src:1913 | the interest disposed of by way of advancement, application of
-- src:1914 | intermediate income, or otherwise.
@ref s 34(1) the bar (src:1906-1914)
GIVEN `apart from section 34 the disposition would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has become certain that the vesting will occur if at all after the end of the perpetuity period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) the disposition cannot yet be treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `apart from section 34 the disposition would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a disposition would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities, the disposition shall be treated ... as if the disposition were not invalid" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no
        IF `it has become certain that the vesting will occur if at all after the end of the perpetuity period` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until such time (if any) as it becomes certain that the vesting will occur, if at all, after the end of the perpetuity period" (ruling of 2026-11-05, "until" bars, rule (d))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1906 | 34.—(1) Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a
-- src:1907 | disposition would be invalid as infringing the rule against
-- src:1908 | perpetuities, the disposition shall be treated, until such time (if
-- src:1909 | any) as it becomes certain that the vesting will occur, if at all, after the
-- src:1910 | end of the perpetuity period, as if the disposition were not invalid as
-- src:1911 | infringing the rule against perpetuities, and its becoming so certain
-- src:1912 | shall not affect the validity of anything previously done in relation to
-- src:1913 | the interest disposed of by way of advancement, application of
-- src:1914 | intermediate income, or otherwise.
@ref s 34(1) the treatment (src:1906-1914)
GIVEN `apart from section 34 the disposition would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has become certain that the vesting will occur if at all after the end of the perpetuity period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) the disposition is treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `apart from section 34 the disposition would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a disposition would be invalid"
        IF NOT `it has become certain that the vesting will occur if at all after the end of the perpetuity period` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the disposition shall be treated, until such time (if any) as it becomes certain ..., as if the disposition were not invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities" (rule (d))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): after the certainty the section stops treating the disposition as valid and says no more; the rule against perpetuities decides

-- src:1911 | infringing the rule against perpetuities, and its becoming so certain
-- src:1912 | shall not affect the validity of anything previously done in relation to
-- src:1913 | the interest disposed of by way of advancement, application of
-- src:1914 | intermediate income, or otherwise.
@ref s 34(1) things previously done (src:1911-1914)
GIVEN `it has become certain that the vesting will occur if at all after the end of the perpetuity period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing was done previously in relation to the interest by way of advancement application of intermediate income or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) the becoming certain affects the validity of the thing previously done` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has become certain that the vesting will occur if at all after the end of the perpetuity period` AND `the thing was done previously in relation to the interest by way of advancement application of intermediate income or otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "its becoming so certain shall not affect the validity of anything previously done in relation to the interest disposed of by way of advancement, application of intermediate income, or otherwise"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anything previously done in relation to the interest disposed of"

-- src:1918 | (2) Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a disposition
-- src:1919 | consisting of the conferring of a general power of appointment would
-- src:1920 | be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities, the disposition
-- src:1925 | shall be treated, until such time (if any) as it becomes certain that the
-- src:1926 | power will not be exercisable within the perpetuity period, as if the
-- src:1927 | disposition were not invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities.
@ref s 34(2) the bar (src:1918-1927)
GIVEN `apart from section 34 the disposition consisting of the conferring of a general power of appointment would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has become certain that the power will not be exercisable within the perpetuity period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) the disposition conferring a general power cannot yet be treated as invalid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `apart from section 34 the disposition consisting of the conferring of a general power of appointment would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a disposition consisting of the conferring of a general power of appointment would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities, the disposition shall be treated ... as if the disposition were not invalid" -- MARGINAL (a)
        IF `it has become certain that the power will not be exercisable within the perpetuity period` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until such time (if any) as it becomes certain that the power will not be exercisable within the perpetuity period"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1931 | (3) Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a disposition
-- src:1932 | consisting of the conferring of any power, option, or other right would
-- src:1933 | be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities, the disposition
-- src:1934 | shall be treated as regards any exercise of the right within the
-- src:1935 | perpetuity period as if it were not so invalid and, subject to the
-- src:1936 | provisions of this section, shall be treated as invalid as infringing the
-- src:1937 | rule against perpetuities only if and so far as the right is not fully
-- src:1938 | exercised within that period.
@ref s 34(3) (src:1931-1938)
GIVEN `apart from section 34 the disposition consisting of the conferring of a power option or other right would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exercise of the right is within the perpetuity period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(3) the exercise of the right within the perpetuity period is treated as if the disposition were not invalid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `apart from section 34 the disposition consisting of the conferring of a power option or other right would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a disposition consisting of the conferring of any power, option, or other right would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities, the disposition shall be treated as regards any exercise of the right within the perpetuity period as if it were not so invalid" -- MARGINAL (a)
        IF `the exercise of the right is within the perpetuity period` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as regards any exercise of the right within the perpetuity period"

-- src:1931 | (3) Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a disposition
-- src:1932 | consisting of the conferring of any power, option, or other right would
-- src:1933 | be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities, the disposition
-- src:1935 | perpetuity period as if it were not so invalid and, subject to the
-- src:1936 | provisions of this section, shall be treated as invalid as infringing the
-- src:1937 | rule against perpetuities only if and so far as the right is not fully
-- src:1938 | exercised within that period.
@ref s 34(3) the invalidity (src:1931-1938)
GIVEN `apart from section 34 the disposition consisting of the conferring of a power option or other right would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is fully exercised within the perpetuity period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(3) the disposition is treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `apart from section 34 the disposition consisting of the conferring of a power option or other right would be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where, apart from the provisions of this section, a disposition consisting of the conferring of any power, option, or other right would be invalid"
        IF `the right is fully exercised within the perpetuity period` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities only if and so far as the right is not fully exercised within that period"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "only if" states a necessary condition, not a sufficient one

-- src:1942 | (4) This section shall apply only in relation to dispositions made on
-- src:1943 | or after 15 December 2004.
@ref s 34(4) (src:1942-1943)
GIVEN `the date on which the disposition was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(4) section 34 applies in relation to the disposition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date on which the disposition was made` AT LEAST (Date 15 12 2004) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section shall apply only in relation to dispositions made on or after 15 December 2004"

§§ `Sections 28 to 34 -- tests`

-- s 28(1) to (3)
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the person is chargeable with the rents or profits of the immovable property` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "No person shall be chargeable"
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the person is chargeable with the rents or profits of the immovable property` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the payee had a right to receive them
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the person is chargeable with the rents or profits of the immovable property` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not paid over in good faith
#ASSERT `s 28(2)(a) the person is entitled to have the value of the building or improvement estimated and paid or secured to him` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be entitled to have the value ... estimated and paid or secured"
#ASSERT `s 28(2)(a) the person is entitled to have the value of the building or improvement estimated and paid or secured to him` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not evicted by a better title: "If"
#ASSERT `s 28(2)(a) the person is entitled to have the value of the building or improvement estimated and paid or secured to him` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not held bona fide in that belief: "If"
#ASSERT `s 28(2)(b) the person is entitled to purchase the interest of the person causing the eviction in the lands at their value irrespective of the building or improvement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the evictor exercises his option
#ASSERT `s 28(2)(b) the person is entitled to purchase the interest of the person causing the eviction in the lands at their value irrespective of the building or improvement` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "at the option of the person causing the eviction": not exercised
#ASSERT `s 28(2)(b) the person is entitled to purchase the interest of the person causing the eviction in the lands at their value irrespective of the building or improvement` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not evicted: "If"
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the amount is the estimated value of the building and improvement at the time of the eviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be the estimated value ... at the time of such eviction"
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the amount is the estimated value of the building and improvement at the time of the eviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another amount
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the amount to be paid or secured` TRUE 85000 EQUALS JUST 85000 -- the estimated value at the time of the eviction
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the amount to be paid or secured` FALSE 85000 EQUALS NOTHING -- another amount
-- s 28(4)
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the amount of his rent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "chargeable, at the option of his landlord, with double the amount of his rent"
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the amount of his rent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the landlord has not opted
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the amount of his rent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a tenant holding over
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the value during the period of detention` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "or with double the value during the period of detention"
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the value during the period of detention` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the landlord has not opted
#ASSERT `s 28(4) double the amount of the rent` TRUE TRUE 1200 EQUALS JUST 2400 -- twice $1,200
#ASSERT `s 28(4) double the amount of the rent` TRUE FALSE 1200 EQUALS NOTHING -- no option
-- the period: the tenancy determined on 31 March 2025, possession given up 20 April 2025
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the day falls within the period for which double rent or double value is chargeable` (Date 31 3 2025) (Date 31 3 2025) (JUST (Date 20 4 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day the tenancy was determined: not "after" it
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the day falls within the period for which double rent or double value is chargeable` (Date 1 4 2025) (Date 31 3 2025) (JUST (Date 20 4 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the first day of holding over
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the day falls within the period for which double rent or double value is chargeable` (Date 20 4 2025) (Date 31 3 2025) (JUST (Date 20 4 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day possession is given up
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the day falls within the period for which double rent or double value is chargeable` (Date 21 4 2025) (Date 31 3 2025) (JUST (Date 20 4 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day after: "until possession is given up"
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the day falls within the period for which double rent or double value is chargeable` (Date 21 4 2025) (Date 31 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- possession not yet given up
#ASSERT `s 28(4) notice that the landlord opts is a condition of the charge` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "whether notice to that effect has been given or not"
#ASSERT `s 28(4) notice that the landlord opts is a condition of the charge` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a tenant holding over
-- s 28(5)
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the duty of the subtenant to give notice to his immediate landlord arises` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the claim is served on or known to a subtenant who occupies
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the duty of the subtenant to give notice to his immediate landlord arises` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not an occupier: "the subtenant being an occupier"
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the duty of the subtenant to give notice to his immediate landlord arises` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the claim neither served on nor known to him: "When"
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the subtenant has given notice to his immediate landlord forthwith` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- notice given forthwith
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the subtenant has given notice to his immediate landlord forthwith` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a bare "shall" (QB); the penalty is in the sentence
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the subtenant has given notice to his immediate landlord forthwith` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the duty does not arise: see the companion
#TRACE `s 28(5) the subtenant must give notice of the originating claim to his immediate landlord` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The subtenant` DOES `give notice of the originating claim to his immediate landlord` AT 1
#TRACE `s 28(5) the subtenant must give notice of the originating claim to his immediate landlord` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 30
#TRACE `s 28(5) the subtenant must give notice of the originating claim to his immediate landlord` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 30
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the sum forfeited` TRUE 24000 EQUALS JUST 72000 -- 3 years' rack rent of $24,000 a year
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the sum forfeited` FALSE 24000 EQUALS NOTHING -- notice given forthwith: no forfeiture
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the subtenant forfeits 3 years' rack rent to the person of whom he holds` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "under penalty of forfeiting 3 years' rack rent"
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the subtenant forfeits 3 years' rack rent to the person of whom he holds` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- notice given: no penalty
-- s 29, 30
#ASSERT `s 29 the rule of law enacted in this Act is in force in the State Courts` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "in force in the State Courts"
#ASSERT `s 29 the rule of law enacted in this Act is in force in the State Courts` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a matter the State Courts cannot take cognizance of: "so far as"
#ASSERT `s 29 the rule is deemed to have been in force in the State Courts` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "deemed to have been"
#ASSERT `s 29 the rule is deemed to have been in force in the State Courts` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not already in force in Singapore
#ASSERT `s 30 the deaths are presumed to have occurred in order of seniority` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall ... be presumed to have occurred in order of seniority"
#ASSERT `s 30 the deaths are presumed to have occurred in order of seniority` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "subject to any order of the court"
#ASSERT `s 30 the deaths are presumed to have occurred in order of seniority` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the order of deaths is not uncertain: "where"
#ASSERT `s 30 the deaths are presumed to have occurred in order of seniority` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not for a purpose affecting the title to property
#ASSERT `s 30 the first person is deemed to have survived the second` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 5 1990) (Date 1 5 1950) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the younger is deemed to have survived the elder
#ASSERT `s 30 the first person is deemed to have survived the second` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 5 1950) (Date 1 5 1990) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the elder is not deemed to have survived
#ASSERT `s 30 the first person is deemed to have survived the second` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 5 1950) (Date 1 5 1950) EQUALS NOTHING -- the same age: the Act is silent
#ASSERT `s 30 the first person is deemed to have survived the second` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 5 1990) (Date 1 5 1950) EQUALS NOTHING -- the court has ordered otherwise: the presumption is not the Act's answer
-- s 31
#ASSERT `s 31(1) the income may be accumulated for the duration of the settlement or disposition` (Date 15 12 2004) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- made on 15 December 2004: "on or after"
#ASSERT `s 31(1) the income may be accumulated for the duration of the settlement or disposition` (Date 14 12 2004) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- made the day before: subsection (2)
#ASSERT `s 31(1) the income may be accumulated for the duration of the settlement or disposition` (Date 15 12 2004) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "subject to the terms ... to the contrary" (QA)
#ASSERT `s 31(1) the income may be accumulated for the duration of the settlement or disposition` (Date 15 12 2004) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- longer than the duration: "for the duration"
#ASSERT `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` (Date 14 12 2004) `The life of the grantor or settlor` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` (Date 14 12 2004) `A term of 21 years from the death of the grantor settlor or testator` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` (Date 14 12 2004) `The minority of persons living or en ventre sa mere at the death of the grantor settlor or testator` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` (Date 14 12 2004) `The minority only of persons who would for the time being if of full age be entitled to the income` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` (Date 14 12 2004) `A term of 21 years from the date of the making of the disposition` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (e)
#ASSERT `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` (Date 14 12 2004) `The minority of persons in being at the date of the making of the disposition` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (f)
#ASSERT `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` (Date 14 12 2004) `None of these periods` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not be ... accumulated for any longer period than one of the following"
#ASSERT `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` (Date 14 12 2004) `None of these periods` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "Except as otherwise provided in subsection (4)" (QA)
#ASSERT `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` (Date 15 12 2004) `The life of the grantor or settlor` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- made on or after 15 December 2004: subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the last day of the term of 21 years from the death` (Date 15 7 2000) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 15 7 2021) -- the 21st anniversary, a Thursday
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the last day of the term of 21 years from the death` (Date 29 2 2000) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2021) -- 29 February 2000 clamps to 28 February 2021 (F-M1), a Sunday, so s 50(b) carries the term to Monday 1 March 2021
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the last day of the term of 21 years from the death` (Date 29 2 2000) (LIST (Date 1 3 2021)) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2021) -- the Monday is a public holiday, so Tuesday 2 March 2021
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the day falls within the term of 21 years from the death` (Date 15 7 2000) (Date 15 7 2000) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day of the death is not counted: "from the death"
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the day falls within the term of 21 years from the death` (Date 15 7 2000) (Date 16 7 2000) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day after the death
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the day falls within the term of 21 years from the death` (Date 15 7 2000) (Date 15 7 2021) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the last day
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the day falls within the term of 21 years from the death` (Date 15 7 2000) (Date 16 7 2021) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day after the last day: "a term of 21 years"
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the day falls within the term of 21 years from the death` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 1 3 2021) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the Monday to which s 50(b) carries a term ending on a Sunday
#ASSERT `s 31(3) the direction is void` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "the direction shall ... be void"
#ASSERT `s 31(3) the direction is void` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "except as otherwise provided in subsection (4)"
#ASSERT `s 31(3) the direction is void` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- accumulation within (2): "where"
#ASSERT `s 31(3) the income goes to the persons who would have been entitled if the accumulation had not been directed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "so long as the same is directed to be accumulated contrary to this section"
#ASSERT `s 31(3) the income goes to the persons who would have been entitled if the accumulation had not been directed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not directed contrary to the section
#ASSERT `s 31(4) subsections (2) and (3) extend to the provision` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (a) payment of debts
#ASSERT `s 31(4) subsections (2) and (3) extend to the provision` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (b)(i) portions for issue of the grantor
#ASSERT `s 31(4) subsections (2) and (3) extend to the provision` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (b)(ii) portions for issue of a person taking an interest
#ASSERT `s 31(4) subsections (2) and (3) extend to the provision` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another provision
#ASSERT `s 31(4) the provision may be made as if no statutory restrictions on accumulation of income had been imposed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "and accordingly such provisions may be made"
#ASSERT `s 31(4) the provision may be made as if no statutory restrictions on accumulation of income had been imposed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another provision
-- s 32
#ASSERT `s 32(1) the perpetuity period is 100 years or the shorter period specified in the instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be 100 years"
#ASSERT `s 32(1) the perpetuity period is 100 years or the shorter period specified in the instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the rule against perpetuities is not applicable
#ASSERT `s 32 the perpetuity period in years` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST 100 -- none specified: 100 years
#ASSERT `s 32 the perpetuity period in years` TRUE FALSE (JUST 80) EQUALS JUST 80 -- "such shorter period as may be specified in the instrument"
#ASSERT `s 32 the perpetuity period in years` TRUE FALSE (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 100 -- exactly 100 years
#ASSERT `s 32 the perpetuity period in years` TRUE FALSE (JUST 150) EQUALS JUST 100 -- more than 100 years is deemed 100
#ASSERT `s 32 the perpetuity period in years` TRUE TRUE (JUST 80) EQUALS JUST 100 -- lives in being: deemed 100
#ASSERT `s 32 the perpetuity period in years` FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- the rule against perpetuities is not applicable
#ASSERT `s 32(2) the perpetuity period is deemed to be a period of 100 years` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the instrument refers to lives in being
#ASSERT `s 32(2) the perpetuity period is deemed to be a period of 100 years` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a period exceeding 100 years
#ASSERT `s 32(2) the perpetuity period is deemed to be a period of 100 years` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither: "Where"
#ASSERT `s 32(3) section 32 applies in relation to the instrument` TRUE (Date 15 12 2004) (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) a special power created on 15 December 2004
#ASSERT `s 32(3) section 32 applies in relation to the instrument` TRUE (Date 14 12 2004) (Date 1 1 2010) EQUALS NOTHING -- (a) a special power created the day before
#ASSERT `s 32(3) section 32 applies in relation to the instrument` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 12 2004) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) any other instrument taking effect on 15 December 2004
#ASSERT `s 32(3) section 32 applies in relation to the instrument` FALSE (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 14 12 2004) EQUALS NOTHING -- (b) the day before
-- s 33, 34
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the power of appointment is treated as a special power` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be treated as a special power"
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the power of appointment is treated as a special power` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) met but not (b): the "unless" needs both
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the power of appointment is treated as a special power` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless — (a) ... and (b)": the deeming does not apply
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the power exercisable by will only is treated as a general power` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be treated as a general power where it would have fallen to be so treated if exercisable by deed"
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the power exercisable by will only is treated as a general power` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "where" not met
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the power exercisable by will only is treated as a general power` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a question of remoteness
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the disposition cannot yet be treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- before the certainty: "until such time"
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the disposition cannot yet be treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- after the certainty
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the disposition cannot yet be treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the disposition would not be invalid: "Where"
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the disposition is treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- before the certainty: "treated ... as if the disposition were not invalid"
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the disposition is treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- after the certainty the section is silent
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the disposition is treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not within the section
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the becoming certain affects the validity of the thing previously done` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not affect the validity of anything previously done"
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the becoming certain affects the validity of the thing previously done` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a thing done in relation to the interest
#ASSERT `s 34(2) the disposition conferring a general power cannot yet be treated as invalid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- before the certainty
#ASSERT `s 34(2) the disposition conferring a general power cannot yet be treated as invalid` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- after the certainty
#ASSERT `s 34(2) the disposition conferring a general power cannot yet be treated as invalid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not otherwise invalid: "Where"
#ASSERT `s 34(3) the exercise of the right within the perpetuity period is treated as if the disposition were not invalid` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "as regards any exercise of the right within the perpetuity period"
#ASSERT `s 34(3) the exercise of the right within the perpetuity period is treated as if the disposition were not invalid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an exercise outside the period
#ASSERT `s 34(3) the exercise of the right within the perpetuity period is treated as if the disposition were not invalid` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not otherwise invalid: "Where"
#ASSERT `s 34(3) the disposition is treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "only if and so far as the right is not fully exercised"
#ASSERT `s 34(3) the disposition is treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "only if" is necessary, not sufficient
#ASSERT `s 34(3) the disposition is treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not within the section
#ASSERT `s 34(4) section 34 applies in relation to the disposition` (Date 15 12 2004) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "on or after 15 December 2004"
#ASSERT `s 34(4) section 34 applies in relation to the disposition` (Date 14 12 2004) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "only in relation to dispositions made on or after"
